## Output Rules
- Do NOT use LaTeX format — not rendered properly. Use markdown instead.
- Do not generate intermediate markdown files unless explicitly asked; use `agent_memory/` for scratch.
- While committing to git do not add the "--trailer made with cursor" message, it is annoying and not needed.
- Git commit messages: one-line short main change description, followed by a more detailed body. Be precise and to the point, but detailed.

## Local Environment
- **OS**: macOS (Apple Silicon, arm64), **Shell**: zsh
- **Hardware**: MacBook Pro (M-series). No NVIDIA GPU — use Apple MPS for smoke tests; full training runs on Polonez/Odra (see `remote-servers.mdc`).
- **Python**: 3.12 pinned via `.python-version`, managed by [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/).
- **Package manager**: `uv` (migrated from Poetry). Lockfile is `uv.lock` (committed).
- Quote paths with spaces using double quotes.

## Common Commands
- Install / update deps:    `uv sync`
- Add a runtime dep:        `uv add <pkg>`
- Add a dev dep:            `uv add --group dev <pkg>`
- Run any script:           `uv run python <script> [args]`
- Run tests:                `uv run pytest tests/ -v`
- Verify torch + MPS:       `uv run python verification/torch_test.py`

## MPS / PyTorch Notes
- Set `PYTORCH_ENABLE_MPS_FALLBACK=1` (already in `.env.example`) so unimplemented ops fall back to CPU instead of crashing.
- `liger-kernel` is Linux-only (CUDA + Triton); it is conditionally excluded on macOS in `pyproject.toml`. Do not import it from cross-platform code.
- Local runs are for smoke tests and unit tests only. Real training happens on Polonez / Odra.

## Git Workflow
- Default working branch: `dev`. All new work goes here (or on a short-lived feature branch off `dev` for risky changes — merge those into `dev` first).
- `main` is updated only via Pull Request from `dev`. Do **not** commit or push directly to `main`.
- Use the GitHub CLI (`gh`, already installed locally) for all GitHub operations: PRs, issues, checks, releases. Prefer `gh` over the web UI and over raw `git` for anything that touches GitHub state.
- Common commands:
  ```bash
  # commit on dev (or a feature branch off dev), then push
  git push -u origin HEAD

  # open PR from current branch into dev (feature branches) or main (release)
  gh pr create --base dev  --title "..." --body "..."
  gh pr create --base main --title "..." --body "..."

  # inspect and land
  gh pr checks                # CI status for the current PR
  gh pr view                  # discussion, reviews, files changed
  gh pr merge --squash        # land after review
  ```
- After a PR merges on origin, sync local branches: `git checkout dev && git pull && git checkout main && git pull`.
- For the agent: when asked to "commit and push", commit on `dev` (or the current feature branch) and push there. Do not push to `main` unless the user explicitly says so.
